# Inviscid compressible Taylor-Green vortex with a slab, Jain & Moin (J. Comput. Phys. 2022)
Base nx:   64
Base ny:   64
Base nz:   64
Max level: 0

# Fluid 1 (slab, |x-pi|<1) and fluid 2: gamma=1.4, pinf=0, cv=1/(gamma-1) so that R=1 and T=p/rho
Gamma1: 1.4
Pinf1:  0.0
Cv1:    2.5
Gamma2: 1.4
Pinf2:  0.0
Cv2:    2.5

# Conditions of the paper: Density 1 = 1 (single-phase test), 0.1 (density ratio 10, the default here) or 1e-3 (ratio
# 1000), Density 2 = 1; Mach number 0.05 or 0.2 (velocity amplitude = Mach number x sound speed of fluid 2 = Mach number
# at p0=1/gamma, rho2=1); Slab half-width 1 (0 removes the slab)
Density 1: 0.1
Density 2: 1.0
Base pressure: 0.7142857142857143   # 1/gamma
Mach number: 0.05
Slab half-width: 1.0

# Time integration: to be chosen. Constant dt; the acoustic CFL (|u|+c)dt/dx is set by the fastest sound speed,
# c1=sqrt(gamma*p0/rho1)=sqrt(1/rho1) in the slab: with dx=2pi/64=0.0982, dt=0.015 gives about 0.49 for rho1=0.1 and
# Mach 0.05 (the paper uses RK4 with dt=0.65*min(dx/c1,dx/c2)). The paper's final time is not stated in its text.
Max dt:   0.015
Max CFL:  0.5
Max time: 10.0
Subiterations: 3

# Output
Output period: 1.0
